# A recorded debugging session, kept so anyone can re-run it:
#
#   flow debug replay examples/loop-accumulate/debug.script examples/loop-accumulate/workflow.yaml
#
# The question it answers is the one this loop's `final_sum` output ends by
# admitting: the fold adds `acc.n` *before* `update:` advances the counter, so
# the last term never lands. Watching one iteration is what makes that concrete
# rather than a sentence.
#
# A line starting with `#` is a comment and every other line is a command, in
# the order a session accepted them. There are no blank lines here on purpose —
# at a prompt an empty line means `step`, so `flow debug replay` refuses one in
# a file rather than walking the loop somebody meant to leave a gap in.
#
# Stop inside the body on the third pass rather than on every one. A breakpoint
# condition is the step's own `if:`, evaluated against the run's own scope.
break term if acc.n == 3
# Run there.
continue
# The carried value at that moment: the counter is 3 and the sum is 1+2, so the
# term for this pass has not been folded in yet.
inspect acc
# The same fact stated as the arithmetic the output's description names.
inspect acc.sum == 1 + 2
# Let the rest of the run finish.
continue
